---
description: Context and token efficiency
alwaysApply: true
---

Use repository context economically.

Do not read the whole repository by default.

Start with targeted search based on the request.

Read full files only when required.

Do not repeatedly read unchanged content.

Do not restate large blocks of source code in reasoning.

Prefer diffs and targeted excerpts.

Do not launch multiple agents for trivial tasks.

Use subagents only when parallel or independent reasoning provides
real value.

Do not produce long progress reports.

Spend reasoning budget on:
- architecture
- difficult bugs
- safety-critical behavior
- ambiguous behavior

Use minimal reasoning for mechanical edits.
